# Windows batch files MUST have CRLF endings — cmd.exe fails on LF:
# it reports path fragments ('rvices', 'ndows') as unknown commands and
# exits rc=255, which silently broke install_autostart.bat (only 5 of 6
# Run entries got written). Pin the ending so it survives any checkout,
# regardless of the local core.autocrlf setting.
*.bat text eol=crlf
